From 696d0c4f9463b0d559fac112d034c6b216553433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:34:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 159/160] webrender: ES 2.0 device, framebuffers and drawing
 without instancing

On an OpenGL ES 2.0 context:
- one framebuffer binding (GL_FRAMEBUFFER) stands for the read and the
  draw binding, and the device's cache of both follows it,
- no dual-source blending, no glTexStorage, no framebuffer invalidation,
- instancing off: WebRender's existing indexed-quads path repeats each
  instance for the four corners, now also chunked for every vertex
  array kind, and no glVertexAttribDivisor call for divisor 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
